{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.543099Z","id":"ef50a675ad3062d19bc151e2bcd835850c57383ff16f3a8e569ae4950d496924","body":{"detail":"The on-device-first listen, the fallback to the default recognizer on an error before any words, the stale done status guard (restarting) and the closing on error_no_match and error_speech_timeout follow the speech_to_text 7.5.0 sources, not observed behaviour. Widget tests use test/support/fake_voice.dart. The macOS preview (tool/launcher_preview.dart) exercises it by hand only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":178},"end":{"line":197},"content_hash":"e14b85232466ee07d11da5108c6b8c43f7702ca3e5709fc70b6d09d18e0cc14e"},"summary":"SpeechToTextVoice has no automated test and has not run on an Android device","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122686Z","id":"519b4592322c8a6e193214b09f5e6056f8acca9af7d717ad3ad90e80ac9d98ed","body":{"detail":"isNetworkCut matches substrings of the messages MessagesApiBackend writes (\"Couldn't reach the Claude API\", \"The connection to the Claude API was lost\") and of the SocketException text (Failed host lookup, Connection refused/reset, Network is unreachable). AgentError has no transport kind, so a reworded backend message makes a background cut fail as \"Couldn't make it\" again; test/platform/network_pause_test.dart pins only the current wording.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"156f8c79642126f23fad88ab053f35078163c802f97197249f6a20c17b2c3520"},"suggested_fix":"Give AgentError a kind (or flag) for no-response transport failures, set it in both backends, and test isNetworkCut against it.","summary":"A background network cut is recognised by the AgentError's message text","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/background_work.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268376Z","id":"20593bbe1876abbb2d21c0b3eadeb87da921800ac45f8f48c3a123224b08df08","body":{"detail":"begin ignores the bool from BackgroundWork.start, and the service stops itself in onTimeout and onTaskRemoved (BackgroundRunService.kt:108-114) without telling Dart. While any run stays in _active, every later begin only calls update, which BackgroundWorkChannel drops when BackgroundRunService.running is false. A run begun while Clax was backgrounded (start refused), or after the Android 15 dataSync time limit, therefore leaves every run that overlaps it without a foreground service, so its network is cut in the background again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"751563c93b1fb70a14fa644e5622172ddb388c1e7e1665f4dae7e034a3e23edf"},"suggested_fix":"Keep whether the service runs (from start's answer, plus a 'stopped' call from the service to Dart); begin calls start when it does not, and a return to the foreground with busy runs starts it again.","summary":"BackgroundRuns never learns that the service failed to start or stopped, so later runs go without it","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:37.268444Z","id":"6c13696f9f3187528b3b8e3b8ac448149d4b0625bbf36ee72b64fba852fff833","body":{"detail":"Nothing ties isNetworkCut to the errors MessagesApiBackend really throws: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart:21 builds the AgentError from a literal string, so rewording lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:159 or :267 (the planned tool-loop backend replaces both call sites) silently turns every background cut back into 'Couldn't make it'. The bare substrings ('Connection refused', 'SocketException', …) also match text the backend copies from elsewhere, such as an HTTP error body. The change is small: add a network kind (or a transport flag) to AgentError in lib/agent/backend.dart:18-25, set it at messages_api_backend.dart:159 and :267, make isNetworkCut read only the kind, and add a test that drives MessagesApiBackend with a failing HttpClient through ResumingBackend. Also the ResumingBackend doc ('nothing was received, so nothing was applied', network_pause.dart:72-73) stops holding once the tool loop publishes during a run; the resend must then resume the loop rather than repeat it.","kind":"comment","references":"519b4592322c8a6e193214b09f5e6056f8acca9af7d717ad3ad90e80ac9d98ed","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"e81a3e9229a13e29f606ba06159018d9c0a3a11bdd90030a43fedc1a3303b902"},"summary":"Fix before this ships: carry the cut as an AgentErrorKind, not as message text","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/background_work.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:19.449305Z","id":"2aa65e19e821bf9ddc751ee3990be9971efb543ba8b175814ca680a91d2a5e4c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d03517e7","summary":"BackgroundRuns keeps whether the service runs: a false answer from start, or a 'stopped' call from the service (refused startForeground, onTimeout, onTaskRemoved), marks it down; the next begin starts it again, and AppRoot calls onForeground on resume, which restarts it while runs go on. A stale answer to an older start is ignored by generation. Evidence: flutter test test/platform -> +37 all passed, including 'a refused start is tried again by the next run', 'coming to the foreground restarts a refused service while runs go on', 'a service that stopped on its own is started again', 'a late refusal of an older start does not mark a newer one down', 'a stop by the service arrives on stopped'.","supersedes":"20593bbe1876abbb2d21c0b3eadeb87da921800ac45f8f48c3a123224b08df08","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:19.449773Z","id":"e1e1448f5256d496133829862c3a4e58029b19b62410c7c78d3711a28df540e1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a9d5f160","summary":"AgentErrorKind.network (lib/agent/backend.dart) is set by MessagesApiBackend when the API cannot be reached and when the connection breaks mid-answer; isNetworkCut reads only the kind. The ResumingBackend doc now says a backend that applies work during a run must resume rather than repeat it. Evidence: flutter test test/platform/network_pause_test.dart test/agent/messages_api_backend_test.dart -> all passed, including 'MessagesApiBackend reports an unreachable API as a network cut, which ResumingBackend waits out' (a real backend against a closed loopback port) and 'network failures are told by their kind, not their text'.","supersedes":"519b4592322c8a6e193214b09f5e6056f8acca9af7d717ad3ad90e80ac9d98ed","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:39.631197Z","id":"031609dec6e4411b79c46e5e4da679578c42494db03e839529232ddee0f78692","body":{"detail":"Every listen through AppServices.voice (built in lib/main.dart as DictationVoice.forSettings) is cued already, so the comment composer in lib/ui/app_screen.dart and ThreadDetail's dictation get the start and stop cues without changes. Auto-start is not automatic: app_screen.dart reads widget.settings.dictateComments (the same setting, so it agrees today), and a new surface such as ThreadDetail(autoDictate:) should be fed autoStartOf(voice) or AppSettings.dictateComments rather than a constant. Tests can pass a DictationVoice over FakeVoice with a recording VoiceCues (test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart RecordingCues).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"fad53a229d22a87318137ff585cd765f72a5a64c2f82801b0f0320b98743a775"},"summary":"Surfaces that dictate on their own should take auto-start from autoStartOf(voice); cues need no code","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:39.631346Z","id":"96c8a30c5e4a7b91ac9b6a1a01a05239d551c6f79f71d116280a775b092d982b","body":{"detail":"Covered only by fakes (test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart). started() is fired unawaited just before inner.listen starts the recognizer, so the 120 ms TONE_PROP_BEEP (android/.../CuesChannel.kt) plays while recognition starts; many Android recognizers also beep on start. Check on the phone that the first words are not lost or misheard and that the two beeps are not confusing; if they are, await the cue before inner.listen or drop the start tone on Android.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"534633e449f88f0de69bca311e71c521b04a9f450ac069efddb9c91cd2cf3543"},"summary":"Start and stop cues have not run on a device: the start tone may overlap the recognizer's own beep or be heard by it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:55.998385Z","id":"9ca0b1548d747ebd2b3c9c7f3106215319768bceea52b4e31a857efb879fb4a8","body":{"detail":"ResumingTurns.turn sends the same TurnRequest again after a background network cut; the cut attempt threw, so MessagesApiRunner never called RunBudget.addTurn for it (lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart, after backend.turn). The API may still bill the cut attempt's input and the output it streamed before the cut, so with up to 3 resumes a turn the run's cost (RunCaps.costUsd) and output tokens can undercount by up to three attempts per turn. Accepted: the cost cap is a safety net, the history is cached so a resent turn's input is mostly cache reads, and counting it would need MessagesApiBackend to report partial usage on an AgentErrorKind.network error, which it does not. Test: test/platform/network_pause_test.dart 'a resumed turn runs no tool twice, is counted once and pauses the wall clock while held'.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"97ad2af28b6c6c011378bdda403b32c8a0e57cbbdefd38dbd8dfa77044fcc8b8"},"summary":"A turn attempt cut by the network is never priced: the run's cost and output caps leave out whatever the API billed for it","tags":["risk:cost","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:55.998455Z","id":"2422b32807c40dfe4faafd46b6a24cd5e96419829c004ea3fb6d7833734a7cbe","body":{"detail":"lib/app.dart wraps only the single-call AgentBackend in ResumingBackend (lines ~322 and ~505). Until the tool loop's composer (AgentLoop/FeedbackWorker on MessagesApiRunner) builds MessagesApiRunner(ResumingTurns(backend, presence, clock: ..., onPause: ..., onResume: ...)), a background network cut still fails a tool-loop run. Two things the composer must know: (1) the clock passed to ResumingTurns should be the run budget's clock, so maxHeld and the paused wall clock are measured alike; (2) onPause has no matching onResume when a hold ends by a cancel or by maxHeld (the turn throws instead), so a 'waiting for the network' notification state set in onPause must be cleared at the run's end, not only in onResume.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"1f3806ec459a92aacf8eb341c3c343d0c07acb45fd16b532cdea215654feee08"},"summary":"Nothing builds ResumingTurns yet: the composer of the tool loop must wrap its MessagesApiBackend in it, with the run's clock and the notification hooks","tags":["handoff","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:55.998487Z","id":"6f38eb184ee07e0c7df84c3d596168c0fc9347d543e5d1f7213dfea1738d5466","body":{"detail":"A held turn stops the run's wall clock (TurnHolds.pauseClock), so without a bound a run whose app stays in the background keeps the foreground service, its notification and the change's place in the queue indefinitely. Chosen: 10 minutes summed over every hold of one run (TurnHolds.held, shared by the run's turns), after which the network cut is thrown and the run fails with a Retry as before. Not taken: a bound per hold (a run could still be held for turns x 3 x the bound), or no bound (as ResumingBackend for the single call). The figure is a guess, not measured against how long people leave the app mid-change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"3f6a580e427e63e361785c6fb00dd5152cdb0146f19f1d1211927d753f63bc3b"},"summary":"The run's holds are bounded at 10 minutes in total (ResumingTurns.defaultMaxHeld), not per hold and not unbounded","tags":["revisit:after-phone-use","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:55.223143Z","id":"0acb9ed2947d9acaad20b60463379cc4093436804ea96d6790fda2f4744633f7","body":{"detail":"Flutter's PlatformPlugin.vibrateHapticFeedback maps HapticFeedback.mediumImpact to View.performHapticFeedback(KEYBOARD_TAP) and lightImpact to VIRTUAL_KEY. Both are the shortest key-click effects, feel alike on most phones, and are dropped entirely when the person has turned off 'Touch feedback' / haptics for touches. CuesChannel.kt silenced() skips the tone in vibrate mode, so in vibrate mode with touch feedback off a listen starts and stops with no cue at all, and with it on the start and stop cannot be told apart by feel. Distinct, clear vibration on Android needs the Vibrator in CuesChannel.kt: VibrationEffect.createPredefined(EFFECT_HEAVY_CLICK) to start and EFFECT_DOUBLE_CLICK to stop (API 29+, minSdk is 29) with the VIBRATE permission in AndroidManifest.xml, keeping HapticFeedback for macOS (which has no haptics for these anyway).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"6552a88100bca06dc117511ab6a9815e5bdb13fd2c47c7c39732de4e0335df4c"},"suggested_fix":"Add a 'vibrate' leg to the Android cues channel using predefined VibrationEffects (heavy click start, double click stop) and declare android.permission.VIBRATE; tests assert the cue name reaches the channel.","summary":"On Android the start and stop haptics are near-identical light ticks, and nothing vibrates when system touch feedback is off","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:55.223225Z","id":"e179493b0535f192d6146b48f7c20918706facece7328e81295eca7b7eff5a1d","body":{"detail":"The app cannot tell whether the device's SpeechRecognizer plays its own start earcon (speech_to_text 7.5.0's Android plugin neither plays nor suppresses one), so dropping our start tone would leave silent recognizers with no audible cue, which the request for clear audio cues rules out. ChannelVoiceCues._cue awaits the haptic before invoking play, so the tone request can reach the platform just after speech_to_text's startListening; TONE_PROP_BEEP lasts 40 ms, shorter than the recognizer's service bind and its own earcon, and a pure tone does not produce words. Awaiting the cue before inner.listen would only delay listening by two channel round trips. A doubled beep on recognizers that have their own earcon is the accepted cost. That holds only while the start tone stays short: a longer start tone should be awaited, plus its length, before inner.listen. The stop tone plays after the recognizer's done, so its length carries no transcription risk. Still to confirm on a phone, as this record says.","kind":"comment","references":"96c8a30c5e4a7b91ac9b6a1a01a05239d551c6f79f71d116280a775b092d982b","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"534633e449f88f0de69bca311e71c521b04a9f450ac069efddb9c91cd2cf3543"},"summary":"Recognizer interplay: keep the start tone, unawaited, and keep it short","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/voice_cues.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:11:00.017459Z","id":"80d3becab0a837decae5eca16172b915a9c0086c478bbf21e61f5f538b3d755b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e5eed2e7","summary":"CuesChannel.kt vibrates through the Vibrator: EFFECT_HEAVY_CLICK to start, EFFECT_DOUBLE_CLICK to stop, with createOneShot/createWaveform fallbacks when areAllEffectsSupported says no; AndroidManifest.xml has android.permission.VIBRATE; ChannelVoiceCues (platformHaptics, true on Android) no longer sends HapticFeedback there. flutter test test/platform/voice_cues_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart: +25, All tests passed (new test: where the platform vibrates (Android), only the channel is called); flutter build apk --debug: exit 0.","supersedes":"0acb9ed2947d9acaad20b60463379cc4093436804ea96d6790fda2f4744633f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
